    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from v1 to v2.\n\nChanges:\n- Switched to `POST /v2/graphql` with a named `Settlements` query.\n- Paginates via `settlements(first: 100, after: $after)`, reading `nodes` and `pageInfo`.\n- Continues based on `hasNextPage`, so short or empty pages are not treated as the end.\n- Deduplicates by `id`, keeping the last version received for amended settlements.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After` and resends the identical request.\n- Restarts the traversal without `after` if the server reports a malformed or expired cursor.\n\nVerification against `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n- `reconciled 1873 settlements`\n- 1,873 rows, 1,873 unique IDs, no duplicates.\n- Results matched the live v1 data exactly.\n- Tested the real pagination path with both 100- and 50-item pages; it handled short/empty pages, 19 duplicate amendment nodes, and an actual `429` retry successfully.",
